    "source_based_senses": {
      "3.22.13": "The person approached is a miser and has the Sanskrit accusative. The nearby udyatam is attached to anādṛtya in the word-by-word witness, so the verse does not give two overt objects of abhiyācate.",
      "3.30.13": "The plural kīnāśāḥ appears before iva as kīnāśā. It identifies farmers in a comparison. The thing no longer respected is the aged ox, go-jaram."
    }
